    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2T5aLZeyqd93VC4qKjXVG6U)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on `main`; independent of every other open PR (touches only the `aerospace` package).\n- If merged out of order: nothing breaks; the two `[[on-window-detected]]` rules are self-contained.\n- After merging: `aerospace reload-config` (Stow already links the file); nothing to retarget.\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Problem:** a PDF opened through the DT Open PDF applet gets its own DEVONthink window (#394), and AeroSpace did not tile it.\n- **Cause (reasoned, not observed):**\n  - The window belongs to DEVONthink, not to the applet (it is `LSUIElement`, no windows).\n  - AeroSpace tiles only windows it detects as standard; DEVONthink's per-record windows can be detected as floating.\n  - `aerospace.toml` had no `on-window-detected` rules.\n- **Fix:** two rules run `layout tiling` for app ids `com.devon-technologies.think3` (DEVONthink 3) and `com.devon-technologies.think` (DEVONthink 4). The id that is not installed never matches.\n- Edited the literate `aerospace.org` (new section \"DEVONthink windows\") and the tangled `aerospace.toml` together.\n- **Limit:** if AeroSpace does not register the window at all, a rule cannot help; the checklist below tells how to see that.\n- All DEVONthink windows tile, the main one too. No CHANGELOG edit (nightly tidy).\n- Not run on the Mac: container has no AeroSpace.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [x] Find your app id: with a DEVONthink window open, `aerospace list-windows --all --format '%{app-bundle-id} | %{window-title}' | grep -i devon`; it should be one of the two ids in the rules (tell me if not)\n- [x] Check out: `cd ~/dotfiles; git fetch origin 444-aerospace-devonthink-tiling; git checkout 444-aerospace-devonthink-tiling`\n- [x] `aerospace reload-config` prints no error\n- [x] Open an indexed PDF through DT Open PDF (Finder or Alfred): the DEVONthink window is tiled\n- [x] Open two PDFs at once (select both in Finder, Cmd-O): both tile side by side\n- [ ] Caps+Shift+; then `f` still toggles a window between floating and tiling\n- [x] Regression: a PDF that is not in DEVONthink still opens in Preview and tiles as before\n- [ ] If the window still floats: `aerospace list-windows --all` — listed means a different app id; not listed means AeroSpace never registers it (send me the output)\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard local edits: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .`.\n- Back to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`; run `aerospace reload-config`.\n- Nothing in DEVONthink or the vault is touched.\n- Fish shell works for all of the above; no yadm steps.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCBxDknUyKheXGLEHP)_",
